  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Held, not failed",
      "items": [
        "A queued / paused session's LLM call is blocked inside the gate until the session is admitted — the llm_execution middleware holds with no timeout",
        "On admission (auto or manual) the held call completes and the agent continues its turn as if nothing happened — no /resume message"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Fail-open invariant",
      "items": [
        "Arbiter unreachable (check times out ~2s) ⇒ treat the session as active and proceed — a dead arbiter never wedges an agent",
        "A crashing gate frame is auto-skipped (fail-open); a hung gate holds the turn until /stop"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Session identity for free",
      "items": [
        "The middleware payload already carries session_id per call (turn_api_call.py:133) — no per-session ports, no per-session wire credentials, no base_url re-pointing",
        "Held on urza: per-session admission state + overrides live in arbiter state; the gate is just a per-request ask"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Open decisions (map #28)",
      "items": [
        "#31 mechanism — this diagram is candidate (b): the in-process middleware gate; (a) loopback proxy and (c) client-daemon sidecar are the rejected alternatives",
        "#32 session ↔ lease arbitration · #33 registration · #34 hold cap + downgrade · #35 admission FIFO · #36 gate placement"
      ]
    }
  ]
